<newsitem itemid="46300" id="root" date="1996-09-11" xml:lang="en">
<title>SINGAPORE: Showpla first half net profit up 11 pct.</title>
<headline>Showpla first half net profit up 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>	   (in millions of S$ unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   0.333   vs    0.300</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)	     0.40    vs    0.50</p>
<p>    Turnover			    61.28    vs   52.60</p>
<p>    Other income/Interest income   0.91    vs    1.22</p>
<p>    Interest on borrowings	   3.35    vs    2.70</p>
<p>    Tax				    0.22    vs    0.43</p>
<p>    Operating pre-tax		  0.79    vs    0.78</p>
<p>    Associates			  (0.61)   vs     nil</p>
<p>NOTE - Showpla Asia Ltd, maker of injection moulded plastic components, said operating environment will remain competitive but it was optismistic in view of its regionalisation plans.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
